From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Lamb <paul@paulscode.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 23:26:55 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Serve the node's own tip header, and index a pruned node

Two changes that let Frigate run where it could not before, neither tied
to one chain.

The tip sent to wallets by blockchain.headers.subscribe was rebuilt from
getblockheader's JSON fields, which can only produce an 80-byte header.
On the BLAKE2b chain every header from 961640 is 164 bytes and the
rebuilt one hashes to nothing. It now comes from getblockheader <hash>
false, the node's own serialization at its true length, and must hash to
the block it was asked for. The approach follows BitcoinMechanic's
frigate-knots.patch in BitcoinMechanic/frigate-startos. getblockheader's
difficulty is boxed, since a BLAKE2b node omits it for v2 blocks.

A pruned node was forced onto the legacy path, which looks every spent
output up with getrawtransaction and so needs -txindex, which a node
refuses while pruning. getblock verbosity 3 carries the prevouts from the
block's undo data, and a pruned node keeps undo data for every block it
holds, so it is now used on pruned nodes too:

- a new index starts at the node's prune height (plus a small margin)
  instead of a height the node cannot serve, says so in the log, and
  records its start beside the database (db/start-height);
- an index whose next block the node has pruned since stops with a FATAL
  line naming the block and the remedy, rather than skipping it: a gap is
  a payment a wallet would silently not see. While a new index has not
  indexed its first block yet, it moves its start up instead;
- a mempool transaction's confirmed prevouts come from gettxout with
  include_mempool false (true hides an output already spent in the
  mempool, which is exactly the one being looked up); mempool parents
  still come from getrawtransaction, which needs no -txindex for them.

btc-rpc-proxy, which fronts a pruned node's RPC, intercepts getblock only
at verbosity 0 and 1, so verbosity 3 always reaches the node, and a
pruned block is refused there rather than served without prevouts.
